                {
                    "file": "platform-mc/terminus.cpp",
                    "line": 439,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Aditya Kurdunkar",
                        "email": "adityakurdunkar2@gmail.com",
                        "username": "akurdunkar"
                    },
                    "message": "Maybe we can stabilise: https://github.com/openbmc/libpldm/blob/9f6b9b3aca29a022c597a87f445d487d8020fe51/src/dsp/pdr.c#L408"
                },
                {
                    "file": "platform-mc/terminus.cpp",
                    "line": 439,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Aditya Kurdunkar",
                        "email": "adityakurdunkar2@gmail.com",
                        "username": "akurdunkar"
                    },
                    "message": "Do we need an equivalent `decode_state_sensor_pdr_data` in libpldm as we have `decode_numeric_sensor_pdr_data`?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "platform-mc/terminus.cpp",
                    "line": 439,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "apuli2",
                        "email": "apuli@nvidia.com",
                        "username": "apuli2"
                    },
                    "message": "Good suggestion, we can do make libPLDM API decode_pldm_state_sensor_pdr() stable and use it. Once its stabilized, we can use that in future. \n\nhttps://github.com/openbmc/libpldm/blob/9f6b9b3aca29a022c597a87f445d487d8020fe51/src/dsp/pdr.c#L408C12-L408C40"
                },
                {
                    "file": "platform-mc/terminus.cpp",
                    "line": 439,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "apuli2",
                        "email": "apuli@nvidia.com",
                        "username": "apuli2"
                    },
                    "message": "Done"
                },
                {
                    "file": "platform-mc/terminus.cpp",
                    "line": 449,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Aditya Kurdunkar",
                        "email": "adityakurdunkar2@gmail.com",
                        "username": "akurdunkar"
                    },
                    "message": "Clean up?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "platform-mc/terminus.cpp",
                    "line": 449,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "apuli2",
                        "email": "apuli@nvidia.com",
                        "username": "apuli2"
                    },
                    "message": "Done"
                },
                {
                    "file": "platform-mc/terminus.cpp",
                    "line": 453,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Aditya Kurdunkar",
                        "email": "adityakurdunkar2@gmail.com",
                        "username": "akurdunkar"
                    },
                    "message": "I don't think we need this as we already have a default name for a sensor.\n\n```\n...\n    // To ensure there's always a default name at offset 0\n    sensorNames.emplace_back(defaultName);\n...\n```"
                },
                {
                    "file": "platform-mc/terminus.cpp",
                    "line": 453,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Aditya Kurdunkar",
                        "email": "adityakurdunkar2@gmail.com",
                        "username": "akurdunkar"
                    },
                    "message": "But it looks like even numeric and compact numeric sensors have this check. Feels redundant. Maybe they can be modified later on."
                },
                {
                    "file": "platform-mc/terminus.cpp",
                    "line": 453,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "apuli2",
                        "email": "apuli@nvidia.com",
                        "username": "apuli2"
                    },
                    "message": "Agree but since return value of getSensorNames() is cpatured directly, Its safe to validate return value before use."
                },
                {
                    "file": "platform-mc/terminus.cpp",
                    "line": 453,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "apuli2",
